.TH LIBRDP-X11-VIEWER 1 "2026-07-12" "librdp 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
librdp-x11-viewer \- minimal X11 RDP client viewer for librdp
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B librdp-x11-viewer
.B --target
.I host
[
.I options
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B librdp-x11-viewer
is a minimal X11 frontend for exercising the public librdp client APIs. It opens an X11 window, connects to an RDP target, presents framebuffer updates, forwards keyboard and pointer input, and exposes optional device and media feature paths.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --target " host"
Remote host name or address.
.TP
.BI --port " port"
Remote TCP port. The default is 3389.
.TP
.BI --user " name"
User name for authentication.
.TP
.BI --password " value"
Password for authentication. Avoid placing credentials in shell history on shared systems.
.TP
.BI --domain " name"
Authentication domain.
.TP
.BI --width " px"
Initial desktop width.
.TP
.BI --height " px"
Initial desktop height.
.TP
.BI --security " auto|rdp|tls|nla"
Security negotiation mode.
.TP
.B --tls-prompt-cert
Show the presented TLS leaf certificate and ask whether to accept it for the current connection.
.TP
.B --tls-accept-any-cert
Accept the presented TLS leaf certificate for the current connection without prompting. This is an explicit trust-policy override for controlled environments.
.TP
.BI --drive " name=path"
Redirect a local directory as a remote drive.
.TP
.BI --serial " name=path"
Redirect a local serial endpoint.
.TP
.BI --parallel " name=path"
Redirect a local parallel endpoint.
.TP
.BI --printer " name=driver=path"
Configure printer redirection with output path.
.TP
.BI --clipboard-file " path"
Expose a local file through clipboard file-transfer behavior.
.TP
.BI --audio-output " [device=name]"
Enable audio output. The viewer uses PipeWire when available.
.TP
.BI --audio-input " [device=name]"
Enable audio input. The viewer uses PipeWire when available.
.TP
.BI --video " file=path"
Enable video output handling and write payloads to a file sink.
.TP
.BI --camera " device=/dev/videoN"
Enable camera capture from a V4L2 device.
.TP
.BI --smartcard " [pcsc|vsmartcard=path]"
Enable smartcard redirection through PC/SC or a controlled virtual source.
.TP
.BI --usb " vid:pid|bus:dev"
Enable USB redirection for the selected local device.
.TP
.B --pnp
Enable plug-and-play device redirection behavior without auto-announcing local
host devices.
.TP
.BI --webauthn " [fido2|fido2=/dev/hidrawN|mock|mock=path]"
Enable WebAuthn redirection through libfido2, a hidraw device, or a controlled mock provider.
.TP
.BI --webauthn-rp-id " id"
Add a WebAuthn relying-party identifier allowlist entry.
.TP
.BI --rail " app=path"
Configure a remote application request.
.TP
.B --cr2
Enable composited remoting behavior.
.TP
.B --echo
Enable the echo diagnostics channel.
.TP
.B --telemetry
Request telemetry packet support status.
.TP
.B --multitransport
Request multitransport packet support status.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LIBRDP_TRACE_CLIENT
Enable client, viewer, surface, input, channel, audio, video, and backend trace events.
.TP
.B LIBRDP_TRACE_TRANSPORT
Enable TCP, TLS, UDP, read, write, wait, timeout, and close trace events.
.TP
.B LIBRDP_TRACE_PROTOCOL
Enable handshake, parser, PDU, capability, slow-path, fast-path, channel, and codec trace events.
.TP
.B LIBRDP_TRACE_LEVEL
Set trace verbosity: error, warn, info, debug, trace, or the numeric values 0 through 4.
.TP
.B LIBRDP_TRACE_HEX_BYTES
Set the maximum number of bytes emitted by bounded protocol hexdumps.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
librdp-x11-viewer --target host --user user --password password --security nla --width 1024 --height 768

LIBRDP_TRACE_CLIENT=1 LIBRDP_TRACE_PROTOCOL=1 librdp-x11-viewer --target host --security nla
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR librdp (7),
.BR librdp-api (7),
.BR librdp-tracing (7)
